      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that's a good start, but i feel like the conservative side sounds a bit one-dimensional here, like it's just \"it's a sin because the Bible says so.\" are there any actual philosophical or ethical frameworks they use beyond just citing scripture? like, how do they address the argument about suffering or the idea of mercy?",
